    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d462">

                <pb facs="0728" n="700" xml:id="pg700"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/9–453: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Republic of China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Rankin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-09-04T18:00:00+09:00">September 4,
                            1953—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>147. T. F. Tsiang has indicated to Chinese Foreign Ministry his alarm over Mme.
                    Pandit’s candidacy for President UNGA.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d462-f1"/> Vice
                    Minister Hu told me Chinese Government understands how desire gratify India
                    after latter’s (rejection from political conference on Korea might lead US to
                    vote for Mme. Pandit but hopes US will not endeavor line up additional support
                    for her.</p>
                <p>Hu also asked me to express Chinese Government’s belief that Mme. Pandit
                    selection would have most serious effect on its interests particularly in
                    connection president’s influence over credentials committee.</p>
                <p>While appreciating good support in UNO received from US to date Hu expressed hope
                    that in due course Department might instruct US delegation to concert with
                    Chinese delegation in finding definitive formula for Chinese representation in
                    place of successive postponements.</p>
                <p>In above connection see my despatch 96, August 24.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rankin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d462-f1" n="1" xml:id="d462-f1-content">
                <p>For documentation on this matter and other elections to UN organs, see <ref
                        target="#pg414">pp. 414</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
